[2026-01-30T13:40:54.965Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Lazy load view components with React.lazy\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:34:39 AM\n\n## Description\nReportView imports all 6 view components eagerly (OverviewView, FindingsView, etc). Use React.lazy() with Suspense to code-split each view so only the active tab component is loaded initially, deferring ~80% of view code.\n\n## Reasoning\nUsers typically view 1-2 tabs per report session. Loading all 6 views upfront adds unnecessary JS parse/compile time. Lazy loading cuts initial bundle by ~50KB and makes first paint faster.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Shell & Navigation\n\n**Description**: Main report container with themed sidebar, toolbar, and navigation. Provides the structural layout and controls for viewing research reports.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/ReportShell.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/ReportView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/ReportSidebar.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/ThemedSidebar.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/ReportToolbar.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/index.tsx`\n- `src/components/layout/ReportModal.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\n- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbdddf83-efc9-404e-b6a3-e0a9e67b2ab3","uuid":"60c8883e-1569-49fb-9ba4-56042922a5ca","isSynthetic":true}
